            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of a painful soft tissue swelling in the thoracolumbar region of the spine of a breakdancer, which caused serious diagnostic difficulty because of coexisting congenital absence of a transverse process of the first lumbar vertebra.</AbstractText>
